  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We start by solving $2\\le 2x+6\\le 10:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & \\le 2x+6\\le 10 \\\\ -4 & \\le 2x\\le 4 \\\\ -2 & \\le x\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/1ad54d12cf04e7142b0bcdd78484d9098fd9ca689f464fc5c03f1dbb0671569f.png)\n\nThen, we solve $8x+7\\le -9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x+7 & \\le -9 \\\\ 8x & \\le -16 \\\\ x & \\le -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/12c34a5af230afb788ddd8c689ef0e9b29c5c5adaf35a1e81099453436cf7f3f.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/bc365364192f3784c565ebcb819a5f37885830f93510029647d39883217987cb.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
